# AlexisWorks Site — Cursor Rules

## Project identity

This is **AlexisWorks**, a minimalist static landing page showcasing indie apps. The live site is intended for **GitHub Pages** deployment. There is no backend, no build pipeline, and no JavaScript framework.

## Core principles

1. **Minimalist design** — Keep the layout clean, content-focused, and visually balanced. Every app tile should be equal in prominence. Avoid adding UI chrome, animations, or sections that do not serve the landing page goal.
2. **Static-first** — All pages must work as plain HTML/CSS/JS served from a static host. No server-side logic, no API calls, no environment variables required at runtime.
3. **Readable over clever** — Prefer straightforward HTML and CSS over abstractions, component libraries, or build tooling unless there is a clear, documented reason to add them.
4. **Small diffs** — Change only what the task requires. Do not refactor unrelated template files or introduce dependencies without updating DECISIONS.md.

## GitHub Pages constraints

- Use **relative paths** for all assets (`assets/…`, `images/…`). Never use absolute paths that assume a particular domain or subdirectory unless documented in ARCHITECTURE.md.
- Entry point is **`index.html`** at the repository root.
- No build step is required to deploy — push HTML, CSS, JS, and images directly.
- Avoid features that break on GitHub Pages: server routing, `.htaccess`, SSR, WebSockets, or npm-only runtime dependencies.
- Optimize images before adding them (compress PNG/JPG; prefer reasonable dimensions — icons ~512px, screenshots ~1200px wide, banner ~1920px wide).
- External resources currently in use: Google Fonts (Source Sans Pro). Keep external dependencies to a minimum.

## File editing conventions

| Task | Edit these files |
|------|------------------|
| Page content, app tiles, nav | `index.html` |
| Tile layout, colors, readability | `assets/sass/components/_tiles.scss` **and** `assets/css/main.css` |
| Other styling | `assets/sass/` source + mirror changes in `assets/css/main.css` |
| App assets | `images/` — use descriptive names (`maconzo-icon.png`, `maconzo-screenshot.png`) |
| Site behavior (menu, scroll, tiles) | `assets/js/main.js` — change only when necessary |

There is **no bundled SCSS compiler**. If you edit SCSS, also update the compiled `main.css` or note in DECISIONS.md that a recompile is pending.

## App tile pattern

Each app tile in `#one` follows this structure:

```html
<article class="tile-{appname}">   <!-- optional brand accent class -->
  <span class="image">
    <img src="images/{app}-screenshot.png" alt="{App} screenshot" />
  </span>
  <header class="major tile-content">
    <img src="images/{app}-icon.png" alt="" class="app-icon" />
    <h3>{App Name}</h3>
    <ul class="app-features">
      <li>Feature one</li>
    </ul>
  </header>
</article>
```

Rules:
- **Never use the app icon as the tile background image** — use a screenshot or a solid accent. Icons belong in `.app-icon` only.
- Always wrap tile text in `.tile-content` for readable contrast.
- Tiles are display-only (no `.link` class) unless linking to an App Store URL is explicitly requested.
- Keep six equal-width tiles (`calc(100% / 3)` desktop grid) unless the app count changes and ARCHITECTURE.md is updated.

## Template files (do not expand scope)

`landing.html`, `generic.html`, and `elements.html` are unused HTML5 UP demo pages. Do not add them to navigation. Do not delete them unless the user asks — they remain as optional reference.

## Documentation maintenance

When making structural or strategic changes, update:
- **ARCHITECTURE.md** — if files, layout, or workflow change
- **DECISIONS.md** — if a trade-off is made, debt is introduced, or a task is deferred

## Code style

- Match existing HTML indentation (tabs) and Forty template conventions.
- Use semantic, descriptive `alt` text on images.
- Keep copy concise — this is a landing page, not a blog.
- Comments in HTML/CSS only when behavior is non-obvious (e.g., why icon and screenshot are separate).
